OL,3,GNEWSAMeal price hike 'taking food out'
OL,4,Aof kids' mouths
OL,5,
OL,6,FA price rise in school meals will take
OL,7,Ffood "out of children's mouths", a food
OL,8,Fbank founder says.
OL,10,FSouth Tyneside Council has approved
OL,11,Fcutting back its subsidy of school
OL,12,Fmeals to 80p per day, increasing the
OL,13,Fprice of a meal from #3 to #3.50 per
OL,14,Fday.
OL,16,FThe local authority said the poorest
OL,17,Ffamilies will not be affected, with 46%
OL,18,Fof children in the borough eligible for
OL,19,Ffree school meals. However, there is
OL,20,Fconcern that families earning just
OL,21,Fabove benefit thresholds will be
OL,22,Fplunged into poverty.
OL,23,APub: 05-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,397,390,260,160,0,100
